# Don't ship the Postgres data directory or local caches into the image.
data/
.git/
# Secrets and personal context. The Dockerfile COPYs the whole app/ tree, and
# Git's ignore rules do not filter a Docker build context, so every secret
# sidecar .gitignore knows about has to be named here too — recursively,
# because the operator's host-Python launchers keep a populated app/.env next
# to the code (the 2026-09-09 audit found the real one one COPY away from an
# image). Only the committed template is let back in.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.template
philosophy.md
backups/
docs/internal/
*.local.md
# Cached ticker logos enumerate the operator's holdings and watchlist.
app/dashboard/static/logos/
cache/
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
archive/
# The front end's build and test inputs. app/streamlit_app.py and
# modern2_native.py serve only the committed outputs in app/dashboard/static/
# (app.js, app.css, shell.html, skeleton.html, tokens.css, fonts/), and the
# Dockerfile COPYs the whole app/ tree, so without these lines the image carried
# the unbundled sources, the jsdom suite and its fixtures, and the esbuild
# script. Nothing in the Python suites reads them. The npm manifests at the root
# are never COPYd; they are listed to keep them out of the build context too.
app/dashboard/static/src/
app/dashboard/static/tests/
app/dashboard/static/tools/
app/dashboard/static/build.mjs
package.json
package-lock.json
eslint.config.mjs
.eslintrc.json
